      <title>The Forgetful CPU (Linux on M4)</title>
      <link>https://yuka.dev/blog-2026-10-02-linux-m4.html</link>
      <description>📝 The m1n1 code writes its entrypoint address to the RVBAR for each core when booting the kernel or chainloading another m1n1. I inserted this into the Linux kernel code very early in boot, and sure enough, I got an ‘a’ after “Vectoring to next stage”. After I commented out this write, the kernel booted to a shell.

